<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — the privacy manifest App Store Connect requires.

     WITHOUT THIS FILE THE UPLOAD IS REJECTED, not warned about: since spring
     2024 an app that calls a "required reason" API and does not declare why
     comes back as ITMS-91053 within minutes of the upload finishing. It is a
     STATIC check over the binary — nobody reads this file to decide whether
     it is true — so the only thing that matters is that every category the
     code actually touches is listed, with a reason code from Apple's own
     table for that category.

     TWO CATEGORIES, AND THEY ARE THE ONLY TWO THIS APP HAS:

       * USER DEFAULTS. Four preferences (the distance units, the symbol
         size, the last search term) plus the five `-PP…` launch arguments
         the probes read. All of it is this app's own, read back by this app
         only, which is exactly what CA92.1 describes.

       * FILE TIMESTAMP. `RideLibrary.rides()` and `ReportLibrary.reports()`
         read `.creationDateKey` to sort and title the lists — of files this
         app wrote itself, in its own container. That is C617.1.

     WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, so a later reader does not "fix" it:
     DiskSpace (never asked), SystemBootTime (never asked), ActiveKeyboards
     (never asked). `.fileSizeKey` is read beside the creation date and is
     NOT a required-reason API — only the timestamp is.

     AND THE SHARE EXTENSION HAS NO MANIFEST OF ITS OWN, on purpose: a
     manifest is per-bundle and needed only where a required-reason API is
     called, and `PippinShare` is two files (`ShareViewController.swift` and
     `PlaceLink.swift`) that between them touch none of them. Adding an empty
     one would be a second file to keep true for no gain.

     NOTHING IS COLLECTED. `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes` is empty because it
     is empty: no analytics, no crash reporter, no account, no server. The
     one network call in the app (`PlaceLink.resolve`) follows a link the
     user has just handed over from another app, to the company that minted
     it — it sends nothing about the rider and stores nothing, so it is not
     collection and it is not tracking. `NSPrivacyTrackingDomains` is empty
     for the same reason, and MUST stay empty while `NSPrivacyTracking` is
     false: App Store Connect rejects the combination of false with a
     non-empty domain list.

     KEEP THIS IN STEP WITH THE APP STORE PRIVACY LABEL. The questionnaire in
     App Store Connect is a separate answer to the same question, and the two
     disagreeing is a review conversation nobody wants: answer it "Data Not
     Collected". -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<!-- CA92.1 — "access information from the app itself, and
				     app group containers the app is a member of". -->
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<!-- C617.1 — "access the timestamps of files INSIDE the
				     app's own container", which is where every ride and
				     every report this reads was written. -->
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
